<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<project xmlns="http://example.invalid/POM"><licenses><license><name>MIT License</name><url>https://opensource.org/license/mit</url><comments>Applies to the jmlx native artifact code, mlx-c, Apple/MLX contributions covered by their existing MIT grants, and the other MIT components listed in META-INF/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, including nlohmann/json, fmt, gguf-tools, FP16 and supervised-lda. MIT notices are also retained there for the opt_einsum algorithm attribution and VkFFT algorithm reference. The reviewed Juffa expression has separately identified CC BY-SA 4.0 terms.</comments></license><license><name>Apache License, Version 2.0</name><url>https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt</url><comments>Applies to Apache-2.0 components identified in META-INF/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, including vendored metal-cpp compiled into libmlx.dylib and the NVIDIA/Filipe RNC Maia cexpf and TensorFlow adaptations. An Apache-2.0 notice is also retained there for the JAX Threefry algorithm reference.</comments></license><license><name>Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International</name><url>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/</url><comments>Applies to Norbert Juffa's covered expression in the reviewed Metal erf and Metal/CPU SIMD erfinv material, including corresponding compiled forms in libmlx.dylib and mlx.metallib. Apple/MLX contributions rely separately on existing MIT grants. No CC adapter's license is identified. See &lt;https://github.com/Alipsa/jmlx/blob/551eebeeb66a80ef3af467a6c1b4995c2a7f7034/jmlx-native-macos-arm64/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES&gt; (scope and redistribution basis), also packaged in META-INF/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES. The complete CC license is packaged in META-INF/LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0.</comments></license><license><name>BSD 2-Clause License</name><url>https://opensource.org/license/bsd-2-clause</url><comments>Applies to BSD-2-Clause material identified in META-INF/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, including Norbert Juffa expm1f.</comments></license><license><name>BSD 3-Clause License</name><url>https://opensource.org/license/bsd-3-clause</url><comments>Applies to BSD-3-Clause components identified in META-INF/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, including pocketfft, V8, NumPy, fastermath and PyTorch (including Metal hypot). BSD-3-Clause notices are also retained there for the Random123 Threefry attribution and CUB merge-sort algorithm reference.</comments></license><license><name>zlib License</name><url>https://opensource.org/license/zlib</url><comments>Applies to zlib components identified in META-INF/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, including ThreadPool and the Julien Pommier NEON math adaptation.</comments></license></licenses></project>